{
  "name": "a contributor sees their own rank and nobody else's position",
  "description": "RFC-0008 §7. ADR-0005 says contributors see only their own rank. Without a dedicated endpoint that number has no home, and the temptation is to leak it into a leaderboard response the contributor is not allowed to read.\n\nThe rule under test is asymmetric on purpose: 'you are 3rd' is your own standing, while 'who is 1st and 2nd' is other people's. So /me/rank carries a position and a total and nothing identifying anyone else — no neighbours, no names, no adjacent scores. A ladder showing who is immediately above you turns the platform into a competition against named individuals, which is the failure mode the ADR is guarding.\n\nRANK IS GLOBAL and survives lapsing — RFC-0008 §1a. Carol has the highest overall score on the platform and a lapsed window; she is rank 1 and hidden from default search, and both facts are reported. Refreshing her availability changes her visibility and NOT her rank, which is the sharpest statement that the ranking is one global order the search view merely filters.\n\n/me/verification and /me/reevaluation-status are the other two self-reads: both make a gate legible before someone spends an attempt on it.",
  "seed": [
    "principals",
    "catalogue",
    "repositories",
    "scored_population"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
          "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
          "github_login": "aliceok",
          "email": "alice@example.com",
          "principal_type": "contributor",
          "availability": {
            "status": "looking_for_job",
            "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
          },
          "overall_score": 64.2,
          "generalist_score": 64.2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Global ranking over all four scored contributors. Carol is inactive and still occupies rank 1, so Alice is 2nd.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Positions and totals only. No neighbours, no names, no adjacent scores — the ADR-0005 rule made concrete.",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "ranked": true,
          "unranked_reason": null,
          "active": true,
          "overall": {
            "score": 64.2,
            "rank": 2,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "generalist": {
            "score": 64.2,
            "rank": 3,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "go",
              "name": "Go",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 64.2,
              "rank": 1,
              "out_of": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Bob is 3rd on depth and 1st on breadth. Both true, and the two numbers rank him differently — ADR-0007 §5.",
      "as": "bob",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "ranked": true,
          "unranked_reason": null,
          "active": true,
          "overall": {
            "score": 60.4,
            "rank": 3,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "generalist": {
            "score": 122.7,
            "rank": 1,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "go",
              "name": "Go",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 55.0,
              "rank": 2,
              "out_of": 2
            },
            {
              "slug": "kubernetes",
              "name": "Kubernetes",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 52.0,
              "rank": 2,
              "out_of": 2
            },
            {
              "_note": "out_of is 2, not 1. Carol is the other Postgres primary and counts even while inactive — the board is global.",
              "slug": "postgres",
              "name": "PostgreSQL",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 48.0,
              "rank": 2,
              "out_of": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Dave's SECONDARY Go scores 81 — the highest Go score on the platform — and carries NO rank. Score and standing are orthogonal.",
      "as": "dave",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "ranked": true,
          "unranked_reason": null,
          "active": true,
          "overall": {
            "score": 58.0,
            "rank": 4,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "generalist": {
            "score": 58.0,
            "rank": 4,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "kubernetes",
              "name": "Kubernetes",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 58.0,
              "rank": 1,
              "out_of": 2
            },
            {
              "_note": "rank and out_of are null. An unranked skill has no position, and reporting one would contradict the standing rule.",
              "slug": "go",
              "name": "Go",
              "standing": "secondary",
              "score": 81.0,
              "rank": null,
              "out_of": null
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "CAROL IS LAPSED AND RANKED FIRST. She is hidden from default search and is still top of the board — RFC-0008 §1a.",
      "as": "carol",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "active:false is what tells her she is hidden. Reporting rank:null instead would hide her own standing from her over a button she forgot to click.",
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "ranked": true,
          "unranked_reason": null,
          "active": false,
          "inactive_for_days": 1,
          "overall": {
            "score": 71.5,
            "rank": 1,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "generalist": {
            "score": 71.5,
            "rank": 2,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "postgres",
              "name": "PostgreSQL",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 71.5,
              "rank": 1,
              "out_of": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Refreshing availability puts her back on every board at once, and displaces Alice from the top.",
      "as": "carol",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "path": "/me/availability",
        "body": {
          "status": "looking_for_job"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "status": "looking_for_job",
          "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "EVERY RANK IS IDENTICAL after refreshing. Only `active` changed. Visibility and ranking are separate things.",
      "as": "carol",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "ranked": true,
          "unranked_reason": null,
          "active": true,
          "overall": {
            "score": 71.5,
            "rank": 1,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "generalist": {
            "score": 71.5,
            "rank": 2,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "postgres",
              "name": "PostgreSQL",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 71.5,
              "rank": 1,
              "out_of": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "And Alice is unmoved. Under the old lapse-unranks-you rule her rank would have shifted because of something Carol did.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "ranked": true,
          "unranked_reason": null,
          "active": true,
          "overall": {
            "score": 64.2,
            "rank": 2,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "generalist": {
            "score": 64.2,
            "rank": 3,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "skills": [
            {
              "slug": "go",
              "name": "Go",
              "standing": "primary",
              "score": 64.2,
              "rank": 1,
              "out_of": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A contributor with no primary skill has no rank, and null is not 0 — ADR-0007. Zero would claim we measured something.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/github/start",
        "body": {}
      },
      "capture": {
        "state": "$.state"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "authorize_url": "<string>",
          "state": "<token>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/auth/github/callback?code=gho_fresh&state={{state}}"
      },
      "fake": {
        "github": {
          "oauth_exchange": {
            "gho_fresh": {
              "github_user_id": 100088,
              "login": "freshstart",
              "name": "Fresh Start",
              "email": "fresh@example.com"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "fresh_token": "$.access_token"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "user": {
            "id": "<uuid>",
            "display_name": "Fresh Start",
            "github_login": "freshstart",
            "principal_type": "contributor",
            "created": true
          },
          "access_token": "<token>",
          "refresh_token": "<token>",
          "expires_in": 900
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank",
        "headers": {
          "Authorization": "Bearer {{fresh_token}}"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "overall": {
            "score": null,
            "rank": null,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "generalist": {
            "score": null,
            "rank": null,
            "out_of": 4
          },
          "skills": [],
          "ranked": false,
          "unranked_reason": "no_primary_skill",
          "active": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A HIRER has no rank. They are not in the ranked population.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "contributor_required"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/rank"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 401,
        "body": {
          "error": "unauthenticated"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "/me/verification is the hirer's view of their own gate. Pat can see exactly why nothing works yet.",
      "as": "pending_pat",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/verification"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "status": "pending",
          "hirer_verified": false,
          "organization": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b003",
            "name": "Unknown Ltd",
            "verified": false,
            "payment_verified": false
          },
          "submitted_at": "<timestamp>",
          "reviewed_at": null,
          "reason": null
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/verification"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "status": "approved",
          "hirer_verified": true,
          "organization": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001",
            "name": "Acme Corp",
            "verified": true,
            "payment_verified": true
          },
          "submitted_at": "<timestamp>",
          "reviewed_at": "<timestamp>",
          "reason": null
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A contributor has no verification. The endpoint belongs to the hirer surface.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/verification"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "hirer_required"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "/me/reevaluation-status makes the ADR-0007 cooldown legible BEFORE a contributor spends a request on a 429.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/reevaluation-status"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Never disputed. tier 0, no cooldown, and the next request is free.",
        "body": {
          "rejection_count": 0,
          "tier": 0,
          "cooldown_until": null,
          "can_request": true,
          "claims_eligible": [
            "01920000-0000-7000-8000-0000000f0001"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/claims/01920000-0000-7000-8000-0000000f0001/reevaluation",
        "body": {
          "reason": "PR 102 was judged as a dependency bump; it reworks the renewal bound."
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "reeval": "$.id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "claim_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-0000000f0001",
          "status": "pending",
          "created_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/reevaluation-status"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "A pending dispute blocks another on the same claim, without touching the cooldown — nothing has been rejected yet.",
        "body": {
          "rejection_count": 0,
          "tier": 0,
          "cooldown_until": null,
          "can_request": false,
          "blocked_by": "pending_request",
          "pending_request_id": "<uuid>",
          "claims_eligible": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "root",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/reevaluations/{{reeval}}/decide",
        "body": {
          "decision": "rejected",
          "reason": "The renewal bound is a constant change; the judgement stands."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "status": "rejected",
          "reason": "The renewal bound is a constant change; the judgement stands.",
          "reviewed_at": "<timestamp>",
          "claim_requeued": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/reevaluation-status"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "First rejection puts her on the 28-day tier — ADR-0007. The number is shown rather than discovered by hitting a 429.",
        "body": {
          "rejection_count": 1,
          "tier": 1,
          "cooldown_until": "<timestamp>",
          "cooldown_days": 28,
          "can_request": false,
          "blocked_by": "cooldown",
          "claims_eligible": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/reevaluation-status"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "contributor_required"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
